  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Basic Education Quality and Access in Laos Phase 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Basic Education Quality and Access in Laos (BEQUAL) Program Phase 1 aims to improve the quality of basic education. Funding will strengthen  critical institutional systems, improve access and participation for disadvantaged children; improve the quality of teachers leading to better learning outcomes; provide basic infrastructure and develop high quality teaching and learning materials to promote reading, writing and numeracy. The program will work in 65 of the most educationally disadvantaged districts towards achieving three intermediate objectives: 1) Participation - more disadvantaged children and young people participate in primary education daily and are ready to learn; 2) Resourcing - learning environments in targeted geographic areas are more equitably and adequately resourced; and 3) Effective Teaching - effective teaching enables more disadvantaged girls and boys to learn.</narrative>
  </description>
